    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d177-a1">

                <pb facs="0338" n="210" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg210"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Siamese Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Traidos</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American
                        Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bay</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName type="venue"><hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Saranromya Palace</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1928-09-18"><hi rendition="#italic">18
                                September, 1928</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. A. 40/12260</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur le Chargé d’Affaires</hi>: I have the honour
                    to acknowledge the receipt of your letter of 27th August last, communicating for
                    the consideration and approval of my Government the text of the multilateral
                    Treaty Renouncing War, signed in Paris on 27th August last by the Government of
                    the United States of America and the Governments of Australia, Belgium, Canada,
                    Czechoslovakia, France, Germany, Great Britain, India, The Irish Free State,
                    Italy, Japan, New Zealand, Poland and South Africa.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have much pleasure in informing you that His Majesty’s Government is
                    in full agreement with the high object of this treaty and will adhere thereto
                    without reservations and I shall in due course transmit, in accordance with the
                    provisions of Article 3, for deposit at Washington, through His Majesty’s
                    Minister there, the formal instrument of adherence.</p>
                <p>In asking you to be good enough to inform your Government of this decision of His
                    Majesty’s Government, I also request you to express its appreciation of the
                    opportunity to participate in this new movement for world peace.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Traidos</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
